            "kind": "docstring",
            "start": 48,
            "end": 59,
            "text": "Return the full deterministic topological order of all changes.\n\n    Kahn's algorithm with a min-heap keyed by change id: among changes whose\ndependencies are already emitted, the lexicographically smallest id goes\n    next. That tie-break is what makes plans reproducible across runs.\n\n    The order is computed over *all* changes, including already applied ones, so\n    that rollback can invert the same canonical sequence (SPEC G1) and plan\n    replay does not change relative order. If any node remains unresolved the\n    graph has a cycle somewhere, including a self-loop, and we fail with\n    ``dependency-cycle`` instead of emitting a partial order."
          },
