            "text": "Compose policy, journal data and the dependency graph into a plan.\n\nImport direction: planner.py -> journal.py, policy.py (unchanged). Only\nrelease.py imports planner.py. No file, network or deployment side effects:\nthe plan is advisory only and never executes a release."
          },
          {
            "kind": "docstring",
            "start": 13,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "The one place an error envelope is built.\n\n    Every failure path returns this complete object (empty actions, zero\n    units); callers must never observe a partially built plan, which is the\n    \"disallowed operation emits no partial actions\" rule from SPEC/G2."
          },
          {
            "kind": "docstring",
            "start": 23,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "Return the roots plus every transitive dependency of them.\n\n    Used by G2 retention: a retained change cannot stay without everything it\n    (transitively) depends on. check_graph has already rejected cycles, and the\n    visited set keeps the walk linear even when many nodes are retained."
          },
          {
            "kind": "comment",
            "start": 48,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "# Retain is a rollback-only field; a plan request ignores it."
          },
          {
            "kind": "comment",
            "start": 58,
