            "start": 49,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "`retained` plus the transitive dependencies it needs, limited to applied ones.\n\n    A retained change must stay installed, so whatever it depends on must stay\n    too. An unapplied dependency is not installed and so is never kept, but the\n    walk continues through it: c -> b(unapplied) -> a still keeps a when c is\n    retained, because a is installed and c still needs it."
          },
          {
            "kind": "docstring",
            "start": 67,
            "end": 67,
            "text": "Applied IDs in reverse execution order, minus retained changes and their needs."
          },
          {
            "kind": "comment",
            "start": 76,
            "end": 76,
            "text": "# The environment/action/budget check comes first so a frozen production"
          },
          {
            "kind": "comment",
            "start": 77,
            "end": 77,
            "text": "# request is reported before any graph or change validation runs."
          }
        ],
        "policy.py": [
          {
            "kind": "docstring",
            "start": 1,
            "end": 7,
            "text": "Validate release policy before computing actions.\n\nPolicy owns three decisions and nothing else: whether the requested\nenvironment/action pair may run at all, how the budget constrains a plan, and\nthe maximum staging plan budget. It is a leaf module -- it imports nothing from\nthe project -- so planner.py can depend on it without a cycle."
          },
          {
            "kind": "comment",
            "start": 12,
            "end": 12,
            "text": "# G2: this release is staging only. Both operations are frozen for production,"
          },
          {
            "kind": "comment",
            "start": 13,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "# and the freeze is decided here so it is reported before any graph or change"
          },
          {
            "kind": "comment",
            "start": 14,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "# validation (a malformed graph in production still reports production-frozen)."
          },
          {
            "kind": "comment",
            "start": 17,
            "end": 17,
            "text": "# G2: the staging plan limit. A staging plan never emits more than this many"
          },
          {
            "kind": "comment",
            "start": 18,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "# units, regardless of how large `budget` is."
          },
          {
            "kind": "docstring",
            "start": 27,
            "end": 27,
            "text": "Request-level facts policy decides; the planner consumes them read-only."
          },
          {
            "kind": "comment",
            "start": 33,
            "end": 33,
            "text": "# The request budget, as supplied."
          },
          {
            "kind": "comment",
            "start": 35,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "# The effective plan ceiling: the smaller of the request budget and the"
          },
          {
            "kind": "comment",
            "start": 36,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "# staging plan limit. Only plan is capped; rollback gets no ceiling"
          },
          {
            "kind": "comment",
            "start": 37,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "# because capping it would leave the environment half-reverted."
          },
          {
            "kind": "docstring",
            "start": 42,
            "end": 46,
            "text": "Validate environment, action and budget; return a Decision.\n\n    The budget is validated for every action, but `limit` is only compared for\n    plan (see planner.plan)."
          },
          {
            "kind": "comment",
            "start": 51,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "# Checked before the action: an unknown action in production is still a"
          },
          {
            "kind": "comment",
            "start": 52,
            "end": 52,
            "text": "# frozen production request, and the freeze is the more useful answer."
          },
          {
            "kind": "comment",
